      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually, the compiler error is correct (and only being allowed as an extension by some implementations) because `std::span` states `ElementType is required to be a complete object type that is not an abstract class type`. So it is not possible to have a `std::span\u003cEnlosingType\u003e` without undefined behavior. Deleting the implicit copy constructor does \"work around\" this particular implementations UB, but this is still UB with `std::span`. `SkSpan` was written explicitly to allow this. See also https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/issues/106988 .\n\nThere may be more of these instances elsewhere that we don\u0027t know about.",
      "revId": "5740cce1f00bbaa316e0c67c2b7a837ca7fc56db",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
